<ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">equip</ansi>

Equip one item from shared company cargo on the leader.

  equip [item]
  wear [item]
  wield [item]

Use an exact reference from company equipment for duplicate names.
To equip a companion, use company equip [member] [item].
Two-handed weapons displace the offhand. Bound or cursed items can block changes.
Character > Gear lets you select a slot, preview Current → After, and equip
an exact cargo item. Pack appears alongside weapon and armor slots.
Gear changes are refused in battle. See <ansi fg="command">help equipment</ansi>.

A class refuses gear it isn't taught: only warriors carry any shield,
rangers only bucklers, and clerics fight with staffs, rods and maces
(<ansi fg="command">help shields</ansi>). Armor heavier than your class's training goes on with a
warning, and costs you turns, dodge, Attack and Evasion (<ansi fg="command">help armor</ansi>).
